    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d10">

                <pb facs="0022" n="10" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg10"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4 Steering Committee/522: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Denmark</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Winship</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-04-29T13:00:00+01:00">April 29, 1937—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 29—7:56 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>12. Department’s telegram 9, April 27.<anchor n="26" xml:id="d10-f1"/> Danish
                    Government in sympathy with convention national defense expenditures made public
                        <pb facs="0023" n="11" xml:id="pg11"/> annually in defense budget regarding
                    control and publicity of arms manufacture and sale, see my despatch No. 565,
                    October 23, 1936.<anchor n="27" xml:id="d10-f2"/> Parliament now debating new
                    Government bill extending control similar to law recently enacted in Sweden.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Winship</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d10-f1" n="26" xml:id="d10-f1-content">
                <p>See last paragraph of telegram No. 8, April 27, 6 p.m., to the Minister in
                    Sweden, <ref target="#pg9">p. 9</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d10-f2" n="27" xml:id="d10-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
